{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"foamy-antelopine-caribou","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Parity sibling discovered by the rebar-debug sweep of `254e-1770-854b-47a2`\n\nWhile fixing the Anthropic LLM transport's zero/expired-`Retry-After` herd vector (254e), the Step-7 parity census found the **same class-B vector** on a parallel, non-LLM surface: the Jira reconciler's 429 backoff. This is filed (not fixed in 254e) because 254e's operator-approved scope is explicitly **Anthropic-only** (\"Bedrock path untouched; Anthropic-only change\") and the reconciler is a separate subsystem (ADR 0036, its own MAX_BACKOFF/attempt policy).\n\n### The finding\n`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_errors.py` `parse_retry_after()` returns `secs if secs >= 0 else None` — so a `Retry-After: 0` parses to **`0.0`**, not `None`. Callers then honor it as an immediate retry:\n- `dispatch_apply_phases.py` `_call_with_retry`: `delay = min(MAX_BACKOFF_S, retry_after)` -> `min(60, 0.0) = 0.0` -> `time.sleep(0.0)` -> immediate replay.\n- `adapters/jira_datacenter/retry.py` `_rate_limit_delay`: `min(MAX_BACKOFF_S, 0.0 * (1+jitter)) = 0.0` (the `is not None` guard passes for `0.0`).\n- `adapters/jira/acli_subprocess.py` `_rate_limit_backoff`: the `\\d+(\\.\\d+)?` regex matches `0` -> `min(0.0, MAX) = 0.0`.\n\nAcross concurrent reconcilers hitting the SAME Jira instance, a server-sent `Retry-After: 0` synchronizes an immediate replay — the identical thundering-herd class B that 254e fixes for Anthropic.\n\n### NOT present here (unlike Anthropic)\nThe class-A vector (non-jittered no-`Retry-After` fallback) is **absent**: all three reconciler adapters already jitter their no-header fallback (`2**(attempt+1)+random.random()` / `+uniform(0,1)` / `retry_after*(1+random*0.2)`). Only the zero-guard (class B) is missing.\n\n### Proposed fix (single-source, low blast radius)\nChange `parse_retry_after` to treat a non-positive value as absent: `return secs if secs > 0 else None` (0/negative -> `None` -> the already-jittered fallback). This fixes all three callers at the shared parser. Confirm the DC/acli inline parses agree (acli regex could also be tightened to ignore a `0`). Add a RED test asserting a `Retry-After: 0` yields the jittered fallback (`> 0`), not `sleep(0)`, per the same held-out RED->GREEN discipline used in 254e.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `parse_retry_after(\"0\")` (and `\"0.0\"`) returns `None`, so callers use the jittered fallback; a held-out unit test asserts the resulting reconciler backoff delay is `> 0`.\n- [ ] A positive `Retry-After` (e.g. `\"2\"`) is still honored (regression guard), capped at `MAX_BACKOFF_S`.\n- [ ] The no-`Retry-After` jittered fallback in all three adapters is unchanged.\n- [ ] `make lint && make typecheck && make test` green; lands via Gerrit.\n\n## Testing\n- `.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/unit -k \"retry_after or reconciler_retry\" -q` (new/updated held-out tests over `parse_retry_after` and `_call_with_retry`).\n- Full gate: `make lint && make typecheck && make test`.","id":"3604-891f-e301-4aff","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":["prevention","backoff","resilience","reconciler","jira","discovered-from-254e"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Reconciler backoff: parse_retry_after treats Retry-After: 0 as an immediate retry (zero-guard parity with the Anthropic transport)"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788131191889105511,"uuid":"ddb2d524-3b30-415b-95a3-2abbf43f73ca"}